{"id":"word:hebrew:H8045","type":"word","title":"שָׁמַד","subtitle":"H8045 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to desolate","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to שָׁמַד (H8045) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 90 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"שָׁמַד (shâmad) means to desolate First listed occurrence: 1Chr 5 25."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"שָׁמַד","transliteration":"shâmad","pronunciation":"shaw-mad'","strong":"H8045","lemmaId":"hebrew:H8045","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["לְ/הַשְׁמִ֥יד","הִשְׁמִ֣יד","לְ/הַשְׁמִ֣יד","הִשָּׁמְדָֽ/ךְ","הִשְׁמִ֥יד"],"morphs":[["HR/Vhc",12],["HVhp3ms",5],["HC/R/Vhc",4],["HC/Vhq1cs",4],["HVNc/Sp2fs",4],["HVhp3ms/Sp3ms",3],["HVhi3ms",3],["HC/VNq3ms",3],["HC/Vhw3ms",2],["HVhp3cp/Sp3mp",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"to desolate","usage":"destory(-uction), bring to nought, overthrow, perish, pluck down, × utterly.","full":"H8045. shamad [ שָׁמַד ] 90 verb Niph`al be exterminated, destroyed (Late Hebrew derived species; Aramaic שְׁמַד Pa`el cause to apostatize (Jastr); Syriac seems disputed (in Lexicons); Nö Eut. Nab. 32 curse ; Ba ES 10 cites Assyrian ašmud , I destroyed ; Gerber 112 thinks verb denominative); &#8212; Perfect 3 masculine singular consecutive וְנִשְׁמַד Ezek 32:12 +, etc.; Imperfect 3masculine singular יִשָּׁמֵ Isa 48:19 ; Prov 14:11 ; 2 masculine plural תִּשָּׁמֵד֑וּן Deut 4:26 ; Infinitiveabsolute הִשָּׁמֵד 4:26 ; construct suffix הִשָּׁמֶדְךָ 28:20 , etc.; &#8212; 1 of person be annihilated, exterminated , Gen 34:30 (J), Judg 21:16 ; 2Sam 21:5 (+ בְּ מֵהִתְיַצֵּב ; — but read ᵐ5 לְהַשְׁמִידֵגוּ Ew We Dr and others), Psa 37:38 (|| נִכְדָת ), 83:11 ; of people Deut 4:26 ( תּשּׁ ׳הִשָּׁמֵד ), 7:23 ; 12:30 (+ מִמָּנֶתךָ 28:20 (|| אָבַד 28:24 ; 28:45 ; 28:51 ; 28:61 , Jer 48:42 (+ מֵעִם . Ezek 33:12 ; Psa 92:8 (+ עֲדֵיעַֿד , compare also מִלְּפָנָי֑ שְׁמוֺ יִשָּׁמֵד וְלֹא Isa 48:19 (+ יִכָרֵת ; וַרְעֶ֑ךָ etc., in || clause). 2 be destroyed , of bamoth, Hosea 10:8 , compare ( רְשָׁעִים בֵּית ) Prov 14:11 ; be devastated , of land, Jer 48:8 (|| אבר ). Hiph`il 69 Perfect 3masculine singular הִשְׁמִיד Deut 2:22 +, etc.; Imperfect 3masculine singular יַשְׁמִיד Isa 13:9 +, וַיַּשְׁמֵד 1Kin 16:12 ; 2Kin 10:28 , etc.; Imperative masculine singular הַשְׁמֵד Deut 33:27 ; Infinitive absolute הַשְׁמֵד Isa 14:28 , יֵ֯ד Amos 9:8 ; construct לְהַשְׁמִיר Josh 9:24 +, also הִשְׁמִידְךָ עַד Deut 7:24 , וֺ - 28:48 , ם ָ֯ - Josh 11:14 (but read in all ׳הַשׁ , as 23:15 , see Dr Deut 7:24 ), לַשְׁמִד Isa 23:11 , etc.; &#8212; 1 annihilate, exterminate: accusative of person or a people, subject ׳י or human person, Deut 1:27 ; 2:22 (+ מִמְּנֵי person), 6:15 (+ הָאֲרָמָה מֵעַלמְּֿנֵי ), 9:20 16 t. Deuteronomy; Josh 7:12 (accusative הַחֵרֶם ; + מִקִּרְבְּכֶם ), 9:24 4 t. Joshua (all R D ), 2Kin 14:16 ; 1Kin 13:34 ; Amos 9:8 ; Isa 13:9 ; 26:14 ; Est 3:6 , 13 23t.; accusative וְשָׁרָשָׁיו מִּרְיוֺ (figurative) Amos 2:9 , compare Ezek 34:16 (but Vrss Co Toy and others [not Hi Krae] אֶשְׁמֹר ); ׳הִשׁ אֶתשְֿׁמִי 1Sam 24:22 (Gi v. 24:21 ), 2Sam 22:38 ; 1Kin 16:12 ; Psa 145:20 ; הַשְׁמֵד as substantive, Isa 14:23 besom of extermination ; accusative אֶתהַֿבַּעַל 2Kin 10:28 , of extirpating Baal-worship מִיִּשְׂרָאֵל . 2 destroy , cities Micah 5:13 , fortresses Isa 23:11 , bamoth Lev 26:30 (H), Num 33:52 (P; || אִבֵּד ), הַגּוֺיִם מַמְלְכוֺת חֹזֶק Hag 2:22 .","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 5 25","keyReferences":["1Chr 5 25","1Kgs 13 34","1Kgs 15 29","1Kgs 16 12","1Sam 24 22","2Chr 20 10","2Chr 20 23","2Chr 33 9"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":90,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 5 25","book":"1Chr","chapter":5,"verse":25,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הִשְׁמִ֥יד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVhp3ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 13 34","book":